# {{PROJECT}}

Created with Galadon on {{DATE}} using the `plugin` layout and the
`{{STACK}}` stack.

This repository is an installable agent plugin: a CLI, a bundled skill and the
docs needed to package it. Distribution files (`.zcode-plugin/`,
`.codex-plugin/`, marketplace icons) are intentionally not generated. Packaging
is a separate gate, and a placeholder icon would pass a check it should fail.

The engineering loop is:

```text
Spec -> Build -> Verify -> Ship -> Learn
```

Start with:

```bash
galadon next
```

## Layout

```text
bin/{{NPM_NAME}}        the runnable CLI
src/                    library and CLI code ({{STACK}})
skills/{{NPM_NAME}}/    bundled agent skill
tests/                  unit and CLI tests
docs/                   profile and packaging notes
openspec/               construction tickets
spec/                   product behaviour facts
wiki/                   knowledge / progress / runbook
.agents/                agent runtime, gitignored
scripts/dev.sh          run the CLI from a checkout (python/node stacks)
```

With the `python` or `node` stack, `galadon.yaml` already declares real checks,
so `galadon check` is green on a fresh clone; `--stack none` ships no checks and
no `scripts/dev.sh`, and fails the gate.

## Commands

```bash
scripts/dev.sh ping --json
galadon check
```
